[gd_resource type="ShaderMaterial" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Shader" path="res://godot/island/shaders/SHADER_horizon_clouds.gdshader" id="1_horizonclouds"]
[ext_resource type="Texture2D" uid="uid://dlulift7s8oa5" path="res://godot/island/textures/TEX_clouds_parallax_band.png" id="2_cloudband"]

; The two-layer parallax cloud band that sits on the horizon in front of the sky.
; Driven by `scripts/world/SCRIPT_horizon_clouds.gd`; every number here is explained at
; its uniform in `shaders/SHADER_horizon_clouds.gdshader` and the shape of the thing is
; written up in `docs/DOC_horizon_parallax_clouds.md`.
;
; THE ARTWORK is `TEX_clouds_parallax_band.png`, derived by
; `tools/TOOL_fix_cloud_band_alpha.py` from the shipped 512x256
; `TEX_clouds_parallax_background.png`. Do NOT point this back at the original: it is
; palettized with a single transparent index, so 82% of its transparent region is
; the raw key colour (teal, 0/92/94) and its alpha is one bit. `fix_alpha_border`
; cleans four texels in from the silhouette and no further, which is enough at
; mip 0 and not enough anywhere else — and this band does not stay at mip 0. See
; the vertical-clamp note in the shader for what reaches into that teal and what
; it did to the picture. The derived file inpaints the whole transparent region
; and reconstructs a soft edge; the opaque region is byte-identical.
;
; The 4:1 sibling `TEX_clouds_parallax_background_2.png` is NOT a clean drop-in, on
; top of every `*_height` here having to halve with it: its .import has
; `mipmaps/generate=false` and `detect_3d/compress_to=1`, so it has no mip chain
; for `filter_linear_mipmap` to select from and Godot will silently re-import it
; VRAM-compressed the first time it appears on a 3D material — block-compressing
; the 244-level alpha that is the only reason to want it. Fix both in its .import
; first. It is also darker and much bluer (opaque mean 129/166/181 against this
; one's 182/182/197), which is the wrong direction against the neutral contract.
;
; RENDER PRIORITY -2. Transparent surfaces sort by priority first and depth
; second, and this has to lose to everything: `SCRIPT_cloud_planes.gd` hands its two
; decks -1 and 0, so -2 keeps the backdrop behind both of them no matter which
; way their own tie-break lands that frame.
;
; THE THREE COUPLINGS, all asserted by `tests/TEST_horizon_clouds.gd` because
; each of them fails as a picture rather than as an error:
;
;   1. Both `*_base` sit BELOW `fade_end`, so the band's alpha is already gone
;      before the vertical clamp could start smearing the artwork's solid bottom
;      row down the sky.
;   2. `haze_color` is the exact neutral 0.30 — `MAT_sky_w2_void`'s
;      `bottom_color`, the terrain's fog colour, the Environment's fog colour.
;      The band's foot has to die into the same pixel the sky already is there,
;      or the palette LUT finds a different entry for it and draws a line.
;      It was 0.089 until the cloud sea arrived underneath it. 0.089 is a value
;      tuned for a DARK VOID; against a mid-grey volumetric sea it painted a
;      near-black bar right across the horizon — measured 0.28 deep against its
;      surroundings, with a 21.8/255 step at its lower edge. It also sat in the
;      widest gap in ps1-soft's neutral ramp (entries at 0.031 and 0.282, with
;      every other step 0.031 apart), so a large flat area of it dithered between
;      two values eight steps apart. 0.30 was found by sweep: it takes the
;      horizon trough from 0.287 to 0.021.
;   3. The node's `cover_up` clears `back_base + back_height`, so the shell's rim
;      never cuts the tall layer's cloud tops off.
;
; PARALLAX_LIMIT MUST STAY UNDER 1.0, and it is a fourth coupling of the same kind
; — it fails as a picture. The parallax model is a small-angle one, and its azimuth
; map folds back on itself once the camera's logical offset passes a layer's own
; `*_distance`: 4.5 km of travel for the front layer, 16 km for the back. Past that
; the band was drawn twice, mirrored, meeting at a moving seam, with the artwork
; stretched without limit along one bearing. It is the tear that was absent at the
; origin and unavoidable anywhere else. 0.5 caps the worst azimuthal stretch at 2x
; and caps the parallax with it: 2400 m of travel slides the back layer 8.2 degrees
; against the unlimited model's 8.6, and the front 20.9 against 30.6. Raise it for
; more near-origin parallax and more stretch; the derivation is in the shader.
;
; BACK IS BIGGER AND SLOWER, FRONT IS SMALLER AND FASTER. Fewer tiles around the
; compass makes the far layer's clouds larger — backwards from real perspective,
; and the whole point: it is what stops the two layers reading as one.
;
; BACK IS ALSO THE LIGHTER OF THE TWO (0.50/0.53/0.58 against the front's 0.38),
; which is NOT backwards: atmospheric perspective washes distance out toward the
; sky, so the near layer reads as a darker silhouette in front of a paler far one.
; Run it the other way — which is where this started, with the front layer at full
; white — and the small near puffs become the brightest thing on screen, the depth
; cue inverts, and the band flattens into a single sheet.
;
; Both tints are pitched against the CLOUD SEA underneath them.
; MAT_cloud_sea_volumetric paints its billow tops at 0.34, and the band has to
; look like the same weather as the deck it sits on; at full white the front layer
; was about three times that and glared over it. `saturation` is at 0.28 for the
; palette's sake — the artwork is blue-and-pink photographic cumulus and the LUT
; will find tinted entries for all of it. It applies to the COMPOSITE, so the two
; tints still separate the layers before it lands, and the back layer's residual
; blue survives as the faint cool cast that is the other half of the depth cue.
;
; The two drifts are chosen so that `drift * 3600 * tiles / TAU` lands on a whole
; number (9 for the back, 40 for the front). Godot rolls `TIME` over every 3600 s
; and a drift that is not a whole number of tiles by then snaps the sky sideways
; once an hour. Retune them alongside `*_tiles`, or accept the hourly hitch.

[resource]
render_priority = -2
shader = ExtResource("1_horizonclouds")
shader_parameter/cloud_band = ExtResource("2_cloudband")
shader_parameter/world_offset = Vector2(0, 0)
shader_parameter/saturation = 0.28
shader_parameter/parallax_limit = 0.5
shader_parameter/back_tiles = 7.0
shader_parameter/back_height = 0.45
shader_parameter/back_base = -0.09
shader_parameter/back_distance = 16000.0
shader_parameter/back_drift = 0.002244
shader_parameter/back_phase = 0.0
shader_parameter/back_opacity = 0.8
shader_parameter/back_tint = Color(0.5, 0.53, 0.58, 1)
shader_parameter/front_tiles = 12.0
shader_parameter/front_height = 0.26
shader_parameter/front_base = -0.1
shader_parameter/front_distance = 4500.0
shader_parameter/front_drift = 0.0058178
shader_parameter/front_phase = 0.37
shader_parameter/front_opacity = 1.0
shader_parameter/front_tint = Color(0.38, 0.38, 0.38, 1)
shader_parameter/art_fade_in = 0.06
shader_parameter/art_solid_start = 0.3
shader_parameter/art_solid_end = 0.78
shader_parameter/fade_start = 0.045
shader_parameter/fade_end = -0.065
shader_parameter/haze_color = Color(0.3, 0.3, 0.3, 1)
shader_parameter/haze_strength = 1.0
